# Chatter standard library: dictionary
#
# Dictionary utility functions written in Chatter itself.

# value_or: returns the value bound to `key` in `input`, or `default` if `key`
# is absent.
#
#   value_or "alice" in ages with 0
#
# Use `input contains key` directly if you need to distinguish "absent" from
# "present with a value equal to the default".
#
# Note: when the key is present, this performs two O(1) hash lookups
# (one for `contains`, one for `value of`). A single-lookup variant would
# require language-level support (e.g. an optional return type).
export function value_or over K and V takes
    K key
    in dictionary from K to V input
    with V default
    returns V
is
    if input contains key
        return value of key in input
    end if
    return default
end function
